# Copy to .env.local and fill in to run against Supabase.
# Leave everything commented out to use the zero-setup local mock store
# (.local-db.json + public/uploads) — see README.md.

# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<anon key>

# Server-only. Required for the developer console's user management
# (creates Supabase Auth users). Never commit the real value.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=<service role key>


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- email
#
# Leave MAIL_USER and MAIL_APP_PASSWORD unset and the portal writes every
# notification to .local-mail/*.eml instead of sending it — the same
# zero-setup idea as the mock data store. Open one of those files in any mail
# client to see exactly what a recipient would have received.
#
# Set both and it sends over SMTP. See lib/mail/index.ts for the full table.

# The sending mailbox. With Gmail this must be an *app password*, not the
# account password (Google rejects those for SMTP).
# MAIL_USER=guesthouse@iitpkd.ac.in
# MAIL_APP_PASSWORD=<16-character app password>

# SMTP host. Defaults to smtp.gmail.com:465 (implicit TLS).
# In production this should become the institute's own relay, which sends as
# iitpkd.ac.in with SPF and DKIM already correct — see
# .memories/09-production-plan.md Phase 2.
# MAIL_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
# MAIL_PORT=465
# MAIL_SECURE=true

# How the mail presents itself. MAIL_FROM defaults to MAIL_USER.
# MAIL_FROM_NAME=IIT Palakkad Guest House
# MAIL_FROM=guesthouse@iitpkd.ac.in
# MAIL_REPLY_TO=guesthouse@iitpkd.ac.in

# SAFETY VALVE — send *everything* to this address instead of to the real
# recipients, who are recorded in the body and in an X-Original-To header.
# Set this on every non-production deployment. Without it, one person pointing
# a staging server at real data mails a real parent.
# MAIL_REDIRECT_ALL_TO=dev@example.com

# Log each message and send nothing at all. Overrides the credentials above.
# MAIL_DRY_RUN=true

# Absolute origin for the links inside mail bodies — a relative URL is useless
# in an inbox. Defaults to http://localhost:3000.
# APP_BASE_URL=https://guesthouse.iitpkd.ac.in

# Right-hand side of generated Message-IDs. Also what threads a booking's mail
# into one conversation. Defaults to guesthouse.iitpkd.ac.in.
# MAIL_MESSAGE_ID_DOMAIN=guesthouse.iitpkd.ac.in

# Shared secret for /api/mail/dispatch (the outbox worker) and /api/mail/cron
# (the daily digests). REQUIRED in production: those routes send mail to real
# people. With no secret set they are reachable only outside production.
# CRON_SECRET=<a long random string>
# MAIL_DRY_RUN=false